# SM354: an append-only changelog should not conflict with itself.
#
# Every branch adds a bullet to the same `## Unreleased` block, so any two
# branches in flight collide there - and the collision is spurious, because both
# additions are wanted and neither touches the other's text. Four branches were
# refused review in one afternoon for exactly this, and the naive resolution
# ("keep both sides") silently DUPLICATED every historical entry whose commit
# ref had been re-spelled by the landing rebase.
#
# `merge=union` keeps both sides of a conflicting hunk, which is the correct
# semantics for a file that is only ever appended to in different places. It
# does not make the file conflict-free in general - two branches editing the
# SAME entry still conflict, and should - it removes the case where they are
# merely both adding.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union

# SM884: the release tarball must not contain the previous release.
#
# release.sh packages with `git archive`, which ships every tracked path unless
# it is marked export-ignore - and download/ holds a COMPLETE release: a
# tarball, its digest and four debs. So each release shipped a copy of the one
# before it, and because that copy contains ITS predecessor, the nesting
# compounds. Measured on 0.14.1's tree: a 34.2 MB archive of which 27.7 MB -
# 81% - is download/, against an engine of about 6.5 MB.
#
# THE TWO MECHANISMS ALREADY DISAGREED, which is what makes this a defect
# rather than a judgement call. dist/config/classification.json:252 excludes
# `^download/` from the release manifest, so the installer has never installed
# these files and nothing in a deployed site reads them. The manifest said they
# are not part of the release; the archive shipped them anyway. This makes the
# packaging agree with the classification that was already there.
#
# Longstanding rather than new: 0.13.13, 0.13.16 and 0.14.0 each embed eight
# download/ entries too. It only became expensive when download/ stopped
# holding the small 0.12.1 set and started holding a full modern release.
download/ export-ignore
